  <p>These terms govern your use of whistleblowerawardcalc.com (the &ldquo;Site&rdquo;). The Site is operated by The Click Lab Agency LLC, a California limited liability company (&ldquo;The Click Lab,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us&rdquo;). By using the Site you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Site.</p>
  <p>The <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> is part of these terms. It states, in short, that the Site is not legal advice, that using it does not create an attorney-client relationship, and that calculator results are estimates only.</p>

  <h2>What the Site is</h2>
  <p>The Site publishes an educational calculator and guides about four federal whistleblower programs: the SEC program under <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/15/78u-6" target="_blank" rel="noopener">15 U.S.C. &sect;78u-6</a>, the CFTC program under <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/7/26" target="_blank" rel="noopener">7 U.S.C. &sect;26</a>, the IRS program under <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/26/7623" target="_blank" rel="noopener">26 U.S.C. &sect;7623</a>, and False Claims Act qui tam suits under <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/31/3730" target="_blank" rel="noopener">31 U.S.C. &sect;3730</a>. It also describes the FinCEN program under <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/31/5323" target="_blank" rel="noopener">31 U.S.C. &sect;5323</a> at a shorter length.</p>
  <p>The Click Lab is not a law firm, not a government agency, and not a whistleblower office. The Site does not file tips, does not file lawsuits, and does not refer cases to attorneys. Filings go to the SEC, the CFTC, the IRS, FinCEN, or a federal court, as the <a href="/#where-to-get-help">Where to get help</a> section on the homepage describes.</p>

  <h2>Not legal, tax, or financial advice</h2>
  <p>Guides, tables, worked examples, the FAQ, and the methodology page are general explanations of public statutes, rules, and agency practices. They are not advice about your facts. They are not a prediction that an agency will open a case, that the Department of Justice will intervene in a qui tam suit, or that any award will be paid. Award law changes. If a page and the statute it cites disagree, the statute controls, and we want the correction: see the <a href="/editorial/">editorial standards</a>.</p>

  <h2>No professional relationship</h2>
  <p>Using the Site, reading a guide, running the calculator, or emailing us does not create an attorney-client relationship, a fiduciary relationship, or any other professional relationship with The Click Lab or anyone who works on the Site. Do not send us confidential allegations. We are not your lawyer, and an email to us is not a privileged communication. We do not agree to keep the contents of an unsolicited case narrative confidential, because we do not want that narrative in the first place.</p>

  <h2>The calculator is an estimate</h2>
  <p>The calculator applies a statutory percentage band to a dollar amount you type, then shifts inside that band based on the contribution and cooperation choices you select. The formulas, thresholds, and adjustments are written out on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> page. You should read these limits before you rely on a number:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The amount you enter is the amount you believe the government will <em>collect</em>. The tool does not estimate the chance that a judgment goes unpaid, and it does not reduce the number you typed.</li>
    <li>It assumes a successful case. Most tips never produce an award, because most never produce a collected sanction.</li>
    <li>For the SEC and CFTC, a mandatory award requires monetary sanctions over $1 million. For the IRS mandatory band, the amount in dispute must exceed $2 million (and, if the taxpayer is an individual, gross income must exceed $200,000). Below the IRS threshold the tool shows the discretionary &sect;7623(a) range instead of the mandatory band. The False Claims Act has no dollar floor; the band depends on whether the government intervenes.</li>
    <li>The tool does not apply culpability reductions, unreasonable-delay findings, a split among several whistleblowers, the public-disclosure bar, the first-to-file bar, related-action sanctions, state false claims acts, attorney&rsquo;s fees, or income tax on the award.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You may not present a calculator result to an agency, a court, an employer, or another person as an official determination or as The Click Lab&rsquo;s evaluation of a real claim. It is not either of those things.</p>

